Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a radio its agent no longer reports is retired

The controller kept every radio an agent ever had. An agent whose radio was replaced (a pod's
USB adapter, or the lab's hwsim radio lost at a pod's re-creation) reports a new radio under
the same AL MAC, and the old one stayed in the model and the database beside it: its BSSes
counted in the topology, AutoConfig Renew sent to it every 40 s for good, and all of it loaded
again at every em_ctrl restart. handle_ap_operational_bss only removes the BSSes a listed radio
no longer has, never a radio the agent leaves out. On rdk-1004 (9 October) the lab's bring-up
refused the topology on such a radio (6 BSSes where the pod's agent reports 5) six times.

An agent lists every radio it has in its Topology Response's AP Operational BSS TLV (an RDK
agent also one with no BSS up). Now the controller counts, per agent, the responses in a row
that leave a radio of its model out; at EM_RADIO_UNREPORTED_RESPONSES (3) the radio is stale.
The controller's manager retires it before the dirty models are written: out of every command
(pending ones drop it, active ones cancel it), its em out of the map with its thread told to
exit (the object is kept: its thread may be finishing an event, and active commands finish
with it), then the radio's and its operating classes' database rows and global entries, and
the model's radio, capabilities, operating classes and BSS rows, which leave the database at
the next BSS list update (0251). A list longer than the model's radios is not counted.

Platform-independent; with the lab's 0251. Upstream candidate after review (a radio's removal
is not handled upstream).

Upstream-Status: Pending

